NOTES=Step 3 PAUSED. Deep read of wasmtime DRC reveals diagnosis was wrong direction. The "leak" isn't missing slot-clear in Kotlin/Wasm codegen — it's DRC's lazy-decrement design + heap-grow-prefer-over-gc heuristic + 4GB hardcoded heap ceiling = pathological on memory-constrained devices. The over-approximation set just grows; auto-gc only fires when 4GB ceiling hits, but device runs out of physical memory + LMK fires first. Fix landscape revised: (A) manual periodic gc — band-aid we know; (B) Kotlin/Wasm codegen avoids per-call SafeContinuation — months of upstream work; (C) patch wasmtime heap-grow-vs-gc heuristic — ~1 day; (D) try mark-and-sweep collector. Step 3 wasmtime patch would only confirm SafeContinuation count growth — confirmation we don't really need since step 2's analysis is solid. Need user input on path forward.
